Attempt 4 failed. The low term `t·(c3·t² + c1)` and the high term `(c5·t + (c7·t)·t²)·t⁴` both land at level 3, but their multiplication histories differ, so CHEHAB rejects the sum. Making the histories match would push the high branch to depth 4, which breaks the 10-level budget. I am reverting to the attempt 1 kernel, the best measured version (639 ms), which CHEHAB accepts.

